# without EscapeAnalysis nothing is noted of what was made here. Link has followed the list, which nobody but the loop gets hold of: its word is held against the list in front of the loop, by a check that stops: there is no arm for a list that is not as made
# PROGRAM-OF: loop-over-a-list-that-a-built-in-has-just-made-has-no-arm-of-the-protocol.ir
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all-EscapeAnalysis
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = GetArrayLength
# RUN(HELD): walk f1 mechanisms=all-EscapeAnalysis
# HELD: = IsPristine {{*}}builtinClass=Array
# HELD-NEXT: CheckProof {{*}}checkedType=true
# HELD: isLoopHead=true
# HELD-NOT: IsPristine
# code that nobody has seen has had the list in hand, so the list is asked
